{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"civil-electoral-lcont","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Outbound clear-assignee cannot unassign on Jira Data Center\n\nFound while writing the row-9 outbound cell of the J11 mutation table\n(story 5200-e04e-246e-4aae). NOT fixed here — filed per that story's rule that a\ncell revealing a product defect stops and reports.\n\n## Mechanism (proven by code path, three links in a chain)\n\n1. The differ's desired value for an EMPTY local assignee is the EMPTY STRING, not\n   None: `outbound_differ._assignee_resolver` returns `(\"\", True, False)` when\n   `not assignee` (src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py:504-505).\n   `assignee` is in `_OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST`\n   (dispatch_apply_phases.py:46), so it reaches `client.update_issue(key,\n   assignee=\"\")`.\n\n2. The DC transport forwards that empty string VERBATIM to the vendor library.\n   `JiraDataCenterTransport.update_issue` pops `assignee` and calls\n   `self._assign(remote_id, assignee)` whenever the key is present — there is no\n   empty-value branch (adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py:281-287, 290-303).\n   `_assign` calls `self._client.assign_issue(remote_id, \"\")`.\n\n3. pycontribs/jira treats ONLY None / -1 / \"-1\" as Unassigned. In jira 3.10.5,\n   `JIRA._get_user_id` starts `if user in (None, -1, \"-1\"): return user` and\n   otherwise runs `search_users(user=\"\", maxResults=20)`, raising\n   `JIRAError(\"No matching user found for: ''\")` when that returns nothing — and\n   when it returns something, it assigns THAT arbitrary user. So the empty string\n   is not an unassign instruction on this path at all.\n\n## Cloud already has the fix; DC never got its half\n\nThis is bug 85a1's defect class, unported. The Cloud transport routes an\nempty/None assignee through `unassign_issue` instead of passing it on, with the\nreason recorded inline: \"Bug 85a1 (Fix D7): assignee=None/empty is routed through\n`unassign_issue` (REST PUT /assignee with `{\"accountId\": null}`) rather than\npassed to ACLI as `--assignee \"\"`, which ACLI silently no-ops\"\n(adapters/jira/acli.py:342-345, guard at :357-359).\n\nThe shape is identical to bug d067 (the status-to-transition seam existed on Cloud\nand Data Center simply never got its half), which the DC `update_issue` docstring\nitself records at transport.py:265-275.\n\n## Expected failure\n\n`tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py::test_outbound_unassign_round_trips`\nasserts `fields.assignee` is null on the DC issue after a local assignee clear\nconverges. It should go RED on the harness until this is fixed.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nGive the DC transport the same empty-assignee branch Cloud has: in `_assign`, map a\nfalsy assignee to `None` before calling `assign_issue` (pycontribs then PUTs\n`{\"name\": null}`, which is DC's unassign), rather than letting `\"\"` reach\n`_get_user_id`.","id":"751e-06f1-bb0b-464c","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"DC outbound clear-assignee never unassigns (empty string reaches assign_issue)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785718531221050001,"uuid":"343dc6a0-b3e4-449f-8986-cd700fd151df"}